WEBVTT

00:00.164 --> 00:03.494
Customer No.

00:05.664 --> 00:09.674
You don't have to be so nervous.
It's not an interview or anything.

00:09.674 --> 00:10.844
But...

00:10.844 --> 00:13.744
You'll be fine. You even got a Lucky Seven.

00:13.744 --> 00:15.004
But...

00:16.474 --> 00:18.704
All right! Take a big, deep breath.

00:22.684 --> 00:26.584
Hold out your hand and draw the character
for "person" three times...

00:30.394 --> 00:31.654
Now swallow it down!

00:33.264 --> 00:36.834
Sorry for the wait. Customer number seven?

00:36.834 --> 00:37.434
YES!

00:37.434 --> 00:38.234
Kanocho
Post Office
YES!

00:38.234 --> 00:39.034
Kanocho
Post Office

00:46.714 --> 00:47.874
I'm counting on you.

00:48.114 --> 00:50.614
Don't fidget, and try your best to stay calm.

00:50.614 --> 00:51.914
Okay.

01:07.194 --> 01:10.724
Something reached for but cannot be grasped...

01:11.834 --> 01:15.704
Something that strays from that hand,
going far away...

01:17.004 --> 01:21.534
People will always pursue such things.

01:22.374 --> 01:25.814
And before long, become lost.

01:31.824 --> 01:36.084
This is our story of one such summer.

01:54.674 --> 01:56.114
Living for the Day
After Tomorrow

01:56.114 --> 01:59.784
Living for the Day
After Tomorrow
The children's graffiti

01:59.784 --> 02:00.244
Living for the Day
After Tomorrow

02:00.554 --> 02:04.214
That has blossomed on the asphalt

02:04.984 --> 02:08.614
Shimmers in the waves of heat

02:09.454 --> 02:12.294
And has begun to walk

02:12.424 --> 02:17.264
At that promised hill

02:17.264 --> 02:20.894
That no one knows

02:21.434 --> 02:26.144
Encounter the miraculous time called "today"

02:26.144 --> 02:30.914
That comes only once - feel it

02:30.914 --> 02:35.084
Chase the flowing clouds

02:35.084 --> 02:39.424
Even now, they seem in your grasp

02:39.424 --> 02:43.794
A premonition, heart beating with excitement

02:43.794 --> 02:48.424
A destiny that has begun to move

02:48.534 --> 02:52.904
So bright that you awaken

02:52.904 --> 02:56.924
Hotter even than the morning sun

02:57.174 --> 03:01.074
Sparkling without end

03:01.414 --> 03:08.714
Embraced in the season of light

03:11.154 --> 03:15.284
A New Lifestyle

03:15.494 --> 03:17.364
Train
Schedule

03:17.364 --> 03:19.494
Train
Schedule
There'll be plenty of these
sorts of errands, you know.

03:19.494 --> 03:20.054
There'll be plenty of these
sorts of errands, you know.

03:20.494 --> 03:24.834
There are lots of things we won't be able to do
unless you become Shoko Nogami.

03:25.304 --> 03:26.564
Here, take this.

03:31.974 --> 03:34.964
Fine. Then shall we go over to your brother's?

03:35.474 --> 03:38.604
Tell him all about what's happened to us?

03:40.884 --> 03:45.154
In any case, you've turned
into an adult, and I'm a child.

03:45.154 --> 03:48.094
There's no way of knowing how or when
we'll change back.

03:49.594 --> 03:51.494
So there's not point in getting depressed over it.

03:51.494 --> 03:53.424
First, we have to get our
lifestyle straightened out.

03:53.994 --> 03:58.124
To do that, the two of us are going to
have to work together.

03:58.864 --> 04:00.094
Understand?

04:16.354 --> 04:20.114
Summer
Sale

04:20.754 --> 04:21.624
Left.

04:22.294 --> 04:22.814
Up.

04:23.424 --> 04:24.224
Right.

04:25.264 --> 04:27.094
Um...

04:27.734 --> 04:29.424
Bottom... I think.

04:29.494 --> 04:31.434
All right, that's fine.

04:32.004 --> 04:34.064
What do you think of these?

04:34.574 --> 04:36.804
They're extremely popular.

05:16.574 --> 05:18.104
Miss Shoko?

05:20.314 --> 05:21.744
Soo cute!

05:22.514 --> 05:24.354
Look, stop saying that!

05:24.354 --> 05:25.484
I was just-

05:27.594 --> 05:28.854
This is cute!

05:31.564 --> 05:33.424
It's too small.

05:37.204 --> 05:37.434
Special Price

05:37.434 --> 05:39.364
Special Price
This is for kids.

05:39.364 --> 05:39.464
This is for kids.

05:39.464 --> 05:42.994
You'll be the one using it,
so we have to get one for adults.

05:45.044 --> 05:47.104
What do you think of this one?

05:47.644 --> 05:51.014
We're having a special sale on it right now.

05:51.014 --> 05:52.534
Let's see...

05:54.884 --> 05:56.714
This one seems just right.

05:57.524 --> 06:00.054
The springs are a little hard...

06:00.054 --> 06:02.884
Well, that's probably to be expected for the price.

06:07.494 --> 06:10.024
S-sis! This one's good, huh?

06:12.864 --> 06:16.394
Y-yeah. I think it is a good one.

06:18.144 --> 06:20.504
Thank you very much...

06:21.474 --> 06:23.464
Now then, as for payment...

06:23.714 --> 06:24.944
Yes, we'll pay for it!

06:26.684 --> 06:29.774
Moron! He's asking if you're
paying with cash or credit card.

06:31.184 --> 06:32.654
W-with cash!

06:32.654 --> 06:34.854
And what about delivery?

06:34.854 --> 06:36.294
Delivery?

06:37.794 --> 06:39.924
He means having it sent to you.

06:39.924 --> 06:42.054
There's no way we can CARRY it back, right?

06:43.834 --> 06:46.434
Um, as soon as possible, please!

06:46.434 --> 06:48.564
Now then, if you'll just fill this out.

06:51.974 --> 06:53.274
Um...

06:57.884 --> 06:59.314
What is it?

06:59.314 --> 07:02.114
Uh, what's your address?

07:05.254 --> 07:06.484
I'm exhausted!

07:06.924 --> 07:11.454
I thought kids never ran out of energy.
Is this what it's really like?

07:12.764 --> 07:13.954
Say...

07:14.334 --> 07:15.694
Where should I put these?

07:15.994 --> 07:19.194
Just set them down anywhere.
I'll put them away later.

07:20.874 --> 07:22.394
I'll go ahead and fold them then.

07:30.514 --> 07:32.484
You certainly are responsible, aren't you?

07:33.684 --> 07:36.184
You're a lot more grown-up than me.

07:36.184 --> 07:37.774
Not at all!

07:38.884 --> 07:41.584
When it comes to the outside world, though,
you're still just a child.

07:51.304 --> 07:53.834
At any rate, you'll have to get used to this.

07:53.834 --> 07:54.994
Okay.

07:59.274 --> 08:01.404
Have to get used to it, huh?

08:16.694 --> 08:17.814
Miss Shoko?

08:23.294 --> 08:25.604
Miss Shoko? Are you all right?

08:25.604 --> 08:27.234
I-It's nothing.

08:27.234 --> 08:29.434
I'll set a change of clothes for you here.

08:29.704 --> 08:31.104
Thank you.

08:31.104 --> 08:32.094
You're welcome...

08:40.284 --> 08:41.114
All right then...

08:41.114 --> 08:42.014
Say!

08:42.014 --> 08:43.144
Yes?

08:48.694 --> 08:51.094
Have to get used to it...

08:54.534 --> 08:56.134
This is so good!

08:56.134 --> 08:57.434
Is it really?

08:57.434 --> 08:58.264
Yes!

08:58.264 --> 08:59.634
Thank you very much!

08:59.964 --> 09:03.334
And those glasses and the ribbons
are very cute on you.

09:04.744 --> 09:08.714
Anyway, cooking really is your specialty, isn't it?

09:08.714 --> 09:10.774
I'd never had goya salad before.

09:10.984 --> 09:12.714
It goes well with canned crab!

09:12.714 --> 09:14.844
Hiro says it takes some of the bitterness...

09:29.634 --> 09:31.224
I don't blame her.

09:36.974 --> 09:38.734
Hiro...

09:40.074 --> 09:42.674
Secrets can't stay secret forever.

09:43.774 --> 09:46.834
Even if we can't return to normal...

09:47.184 --> 09:49.154
Even if he doesn't believe us...

09:51.654 --> 09:54.854
Hiro
Oikawa

10:00.734 --> 10:04.224
Sasazuka
Pharmacy

10:06.464 --> 10:07.504
Thanks very much.

10:07.504 --> 10:08.634
Bye-bye!

10:08.634 --> 10:09.794
Take care.

10:12.774 --> 10:14.974
You should follow your own advice.

10:15.344 --> 10:18.804
You don't look well. You're not
fully recovered, don't you think?

10:22.254 --> 10:23.844
I'm going to go eat.

10:25.484 --> 10:27.144
See you soon.

10:32.394 --> 10:34.524
Still nothing from the police?

10:35.194 --> 10:37.324
No. Nothing yet.

10:40.434 --> 10:41.864
Tetsu...

10:44.674 --> 10:46.004
I'm hungry!

10:46.004 --> 10:47.374
Sis! Shrimp pilaf me!

10:47.374 --> 10:48.814
What's with you, all of a sudden?

10:48.814 --> 10:51.984
I've been out running around this whole time!
That makes ya hungry!

10:51.984 --> 10:57.644
The park, the pool, the library, shrines...
there are still lots more places to look!

10:58.024 --> 10:59.354
Thank you.

11:00.424 --> 11:03.054
Hey... Don't you think she's just run away?

11:04.024 --> 11:07.024
Like, you did somethin' terrible
to hurt her feelings.

11:07.024 --> 11:08.734
What are you talking about?!

11:08.734 --> 11:10.034
Man, that HURT!

11:10.034 --> 11:11.834
It's your own fault for talking like an idiot!

11:11.834 --> 11:14.104
Hiro wouldn't do something like that, would he?

11:14.104 --> 11:16.404
Still, that's no reason to go hitting me!

11:19.104 --> 11:20.594
They look very good on you.

11:21.644 --> 11:23.334
Very childlike.

11:24.314 --> 11:26.344
Apologize to Hiro.

11:26.344 --> 11:28.074
How come I gotta apologize?

11:28.914 --> 11:30.114
Excuse me!

11:30.114 --> 11:31.654
Yes, come in.

11:31.654 --> 11:33.654
Do you mind if I ask some directions?

11:33.654 --> 11:33.954
Delivery Slip
Do you mind if I ask some directions?

11:33.954 --> 11:36.224
Delivery Slip
I'm not familiar with this area...

11:42.394 --> 11:43.594
DIY Bed

11:43.594 --> 11:44.934
DIY Bed
All right!

11:44.934 --> 11:46.424
DIY Bed

11:47.674 --> 11:48.864
That was faster than...

12:03.814 --> 12:05.024
Those ribbons...

12:05.024 --> 12:06.284
How did you know where?

12:08.324 --> 12:10.154
Um, who are you?

12:10.154 --> 12:12.464
Oh, uh...

12:12.464 --> 12:15.364
This is Shoko Nogami's apartment, isn't it?

12:15.364 --> 12:16.634
Y-yes.

12:16.634 --> 12:18.934
I'm a friend of hers.

12:18.934 --> 12:21.424
Uh, Sis is out right now.

12:22.304 --> 12:25.074
"Sis"? So then you're...

12:25.074 --> 12:27.474
Sh-Shoko's younger sister.

12:27.474 --> 12:29.174
N-nice to meet you.

12:29.174 --> 12:31.914
When do you think your sister will be back?

12:31.914 --> 12:33.244
I don't know...

12:33.244 --> 12:37.114
Oh. Then I'll drop by again.

12:40.084 --> 12:41.114
Um!

12:45.724 --> 12:47.214
Thanks very much.

12:49.634 --> 12:50.704
Please.

12:50.704 --> 12:51.764
Thank you.

12:51.764 --> 12:53.024
Not at all.

12:59.444 --> 13:00.404
Uh...

13:00.404 --> 13:01.374
Yes?

13:01.374 --> 13:04.344
Do you happen to know where
your sister went shopping?

13:04.344 --> 13:07.854
I don't know. She goes different places
depending on the day.

13:07.854 --> 13:09.184
Oh...

13:23.994 --> 13:25.004
Thank you.

13:25.004 --> 13:27.964
No problem. My sister smokes, too.

13:32.774 --> 13:35.474
Sorry. I think I'd better use your veranda.

13:50.054 --> 13:51.284
Um!

13:52.194 --> 13:53.554
Actually...

13:58.404 --> 14:00.994
Uh, actually...

14:01.634 --> 14:03.334
Aren't you hungry?

14:03.974 --> 14:06.144
They're only yesterday's leftovers, but...

14:06.144 --> 14:08.014
I'm actually in a hurry, so...

14:08.014 --> 14:08.314
Wait just a moment.
I'm actually in a hurry, so...

14:08.314 --> 14:09.274
Wait just a moment.

14:16.714 --> 14:20.284
Wow! You're so young,
but you can already cook.

14:20.284 --> 14:21.324
Huh?

14:21.324 --> 14:23.794
Your sister doesn't cook for you, does she?

14:24.824 --> 14:26.224
S-she made this.

14:37.104 --> 14:40.274
Say, you and your sister live together?

14:40.274 --> 14:42.414
Yes. Why do you ask?

14:42.414 --> 14:45.244
I just don't remember her liking things so neat.

14:46.384 --> 14:49.114
She's got a new boyfriend.

14:50.514 --> 14:54.614
So she learned how to cook
and started keeping things clean.

14:54.824 --> 14:58.224
She said she had a really hard time of it
with her last boyfriend

14:58.224 --> 15:00.714
because he was such a good-for-nothing loser.

15:09.204 --> 15:10.794
Yes, hello?

15:11.774 --> 15:14.744
"Sakura fish floss"? What the heck is that?

15:15.444 --> 15:16.534
Okay.

15:17.244 --> 15:18.334
Okay.

15:18.914 --> 15:21.314
Got it. See you.

15:22.314 --> 15:25.924
That was my sister. It looks like
she's running a bit late.

15:25.924 --> 15:26.624
Say...

15:26.624 --> 15:27.354
Yes?

15:27.354 --> 15:29.924
About that "good-for-nothing loser"...

15:29.924 --> 15:31.184
Yes?

15:31.364 --> 15:33.524
Which of your sister's boyfriends was he?

15:34.934 --> 15:36.194
Idiot.

15:36.934 --> 15:38.164
Thank you for the food.

15:42.674 --> 15:44.944
This croquette is like my younger sister's.

15:44.944 --> 15:46.844
What do you want with my sister?

15:47.774 --> 15:50.144
My sister hasn't come home yet.

15:51.414 --> 15:57.044
It's nothing I can ask you about, but I was
wondering if maybe your sister knew something.

15:58.324 --> 16:00.654
You're quite worried about her, aren't you?

16:02.624 --> 16:04.054
Yes, I am.

16:04.664 --> 16:06.654
My sister is important to me.

16:07.024 --> 16:08.424
More important than a promise?

16:09.564 --> 16:11.194
Than a girlfriend?

16:16.134 --> 16:18.144
Did your sister tell you something?

16:18.144 --> 16:19.244
Not really.

16:19.244 --> 16:23.044
Just that she was relieved she could
break up with that good-for-nothing loser.

16:23.844 --> 16:25.644
That must be me she was talking about.

16:27.084 --> 16:28.984
You're like your older sister.

16:29.484 --> 16:30.854
What's that supposed to mean?

16:31.154 --> 16:32.524
You're strong-willed,

16:32.524 --> 16:34.454
you've got a sharp tongue,

16:34.794 --> 16:36.284
and you haven't got an ounce of "cuteness."

16:36.654 --> 16:37.994
I got sick of hearing it.

16:37.994 --> 16:39.594
So you have been called cute.

16:39.594 --> 16:41.524
By a good-for-nothing loser.

16:42.694 --> 16:45.924
I didn't know Shoko had
a younger sister like you.

16:47.334 --> 16:51.504
And I didn't have a clue about yours either! Idiot!

16:51.504 --> 16:52.734
H-hey!

16:58.884 --> 17:00.004
Hey!

17:01.114 --> 17:03.014
Wait! Hey!

17:03.454 --> 17:04.784
I said wait!

17:04.924 --> 17:06.714
I'm sorry.

17:08.794 --> 17:10.454
"I won't be coming back to America."

17:11.564 --> 17:13.924
"I don't expect you to come to Japan either."

17:14.734 --> 17:18.794
"You're still a student, and there are things
over there that you want to do."

17:19.164 --> 17:22.264
"I can't have you sacrifice that for my sake."

17:22.674 --> 17:25.764
"Let's you and I move forward
on separate paths"!

18:32.244 --> 18:34.234
Yes. Yes.

18:35.474 --> 18:37.344
Thank you for everything.

18:38.114 --> 18:39.644
Yes.

18:39.644 --> 18:41.114
I will return soon as well.

18:50.254 --> 18:52.094
I'll be back soon.

19:20.724 --> 19:22.654
I won't be coming back to America.
I don't expect you to come to Japan either.

19:28.564 --> 19:32.624
And just like that, you were gone from my life.

19:33.804 --> 19:35.324
Shoko?

19:39.544 --> 19:41.374
Did you hear that from Shoko, too?

19:44.514 --> 19:47.644
If she has a problem with me,
she can tell me directly.

19:47.644 --> 19:49.544
Karada's got nothing to do with it!

19:49.654 --> 19:52.154
If your little sister's that important to you,

19:52.154 --> 19:55.124
why don't you try asking something
from the wishing stones there?

19:55.494 --> 19:57.494
She asked the stones, too.

19:57.494 --> 20:00.224
She wanted them to make her an adult.

20:00.494 --> 20:04.734
And like some kind of trade-off...

20:04.734 --> 20:07.164
Even though I didn't wish for anything...

20:07.164 --> 20:08.674
I became a child...

20:08.674 --> 20:11.674
Enough of this nonsense!
That's not what this is about.

20:11.674 --> 20:14.614
Where is my sister?!
Those are her ribbons, aren't they?

20:14.614 --> 20:16.874
You know where Karada is, don't you?!

20:29.654 --> 20:30.884
Why?

20:31.564 --> 20:33.684
Why can't my hands reach?!

20:35.994 --> 20:39.164
Idiot! Good-for-nothing!
Lunkhead! Irresponsible!

20:39.164 --> 20:42.304
Why don't you get it?! I'm Shoko!

20:42.304 --> 20:46.034
Shoko Nogami! Why do only talk
about your sister?!

20:48.774 --> 20:50.574
She's not my real sister.

20:52.744 --> 20:54.784
She's a relative.

20:54.784 --> 20:58.444
Her mom died when she was two
and we ended up taking her in.

20:58.854 --> 21:02.014
She doesn't know we're not blood-related.

21:02.654 --> 21:07.224
I went to study abroad soon afterward,
so it's not like we shared any memories.

21:07.724 --> 21:10.564
Honestly, I didn't even think of her as my sister.

21:11.934 --> 21:16.094
That's why I didn't tell your sister about her.

21:16.234 --> 21:20.034
And I planned to go back to America
as soon as the funeral was over.

21:21.614 --> 21:24.514
But I couldn't just abandon her.

21:25.214 --> 21:30.744
She came up to me at the funeral,
alone, holding back tears...

21:33.554 --> 21:35.544
Karada is my sister.

21:35.694 --> 21:38.994
My dear, one-and-only sister.

21:41.394 --> 21:43.294
Welcome back, Miss Shoko!

21:44.934 --> 21:48.194
Now, now, you have to close the door properly!

21:51.174 --> 21:53.104
That's your sister.

22:04.654 --> 22:08.484
P-pleased to meet you. I'm Karada lokawa.

22:09.294 --> 22:10.284
Big brother!

22:14.864 --> 22:21.104
Wearing unfamiliar shoes

22:21.104 --> 22:25.834
Each step a pain that I endure

22:27.274 --> 22:33.544
And yet I walk

22:33.544 --> 22:38.344
Because I have a place to return to

22:39.124 --> 22:47.264
I stare at myself

22:47.264 --> 22:51.854
And notice something I'd lost

22:55.004 --> 23:01.174
I want to be with you

23:01.174 --> 23:07.884
To feel it, near and far

23:07.884 --> 23:13.754
To keep creating each normal day

23:13.754 --> 23:20.394
With you, my beloved

23:20.394 --> 23:27.824
To say "I'm home,"
remove my shoes and hold you

23:28.074 --> 23:32.904
My sweet home

23:45.484 --> 23:49.544
The first time I met Hiro was at the funeral.

23:50.124 --> 23:54.684
His hands were so big and his eyes so kind.

23:55.364 --> 23:58.454
From then on, the two of us
were always together.

23:59.264 --> 24:02.324
Do you remember it? That night...

24:02.504 --> 24:06.604
You put me on your shoulders and
we looked up at the night sky together.

24:07.074 --> 24:09.414
Next time, on Living for the Day After Tomorrow:

24:09.414 --> 24:09.644
Next episode
I Want You to Believe
Next time, on Living for the Day After Tomorrow:

24:09.644 --> 24:11.274
Next episode
I Want You to Believe
"I Want You to Believe"

24:11.274 --> 24:13.004
Next episode
I Want You to Believe
